WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.166 --> 00:00:01.292
- Do you think it ended your career?

00:00:01.292 --> 00:00:04.254
- 100 percent. 100 percent. 

00:00:04.254 --> 00:00:05.797
And it ain’t have nothin’ to do with my age, 

00:00:05.797 --> 00:00:08.550
it ain’t have nothin’ to do with my style of play: 

00:00:08.550 --> 00:00:09.884
It was because I took a knee.

00:00:09.884 --> 00:00:14.139
♪♪♪

00:00:17.434 --> 00:00:18.393
What’s happenin’, man?

00:00:18.393 --> 00:00:19.352
- Antonio Cromartie! 

00:00:19.978 --> 00:00:20.729
- What’s good witcha?

00:00:20.729 --> 00:00:21.271
- How you doin’, man?

00:00:21.271 --> 00:00:22.063
- Man, I can’t call it.

00:00:22.063 --> 00:00:24.107
- Since you in my crib, I’mma be an honest guest 

00:00:24.107 --> 00:00:25.066
and go ahead—a generous guest—

00:00:25.066 --> 00:00:26.026
- Yo crib?

00:00:26.026 --> 00:00:27.902
- Whatever, you can go ahead and rack for me real quick.

00:00:27.902 --> 00:00:28.194
- Oh.

00:00:28.194 --> 00:00:29.029
- Some chalk, you need some?

00:00:29.029 --> 00:00:29.863
- I don’t even need no chalk.

00:00:29.863 --> 00:00:30.321
- Oh, you don’t need no chalk?

00:00:30.321 --> 00:00:30.905
- Nah, man.

00:00:30.905 --> 00:00:31.364
- Gonna chalk it up.

00:00:31.364 --> 00:00:32.991
- For what? For you to get beat anyway?

00:00:32.991 --> 00:00:34.492
- Go ahead, bro. Talkin’ all that noise.

00:00:34.492 --> 00:00:35.660
- Yeahhh, buddy.

00:00:35.660 --> 00:00:36.953
- Everybody’ll talk noise, but—

00:00:36.953 --> 00:00:38.496
- Yep, we talk a lil’ noise. 

00:00:38.496 --> 00:00:40.415
That’s what us Florida boys do.

00:00:40.582 --> 00:00:42.000
- In 2016, you’re with the Colts. 

00:00:42.000 --> 00:00:43.918
That’s the same year Colin Kaepernick took a knee 

00:00:43.918 --> 00:00:46.921
to protest police brutality and social injustice. 

00:00:46.921 --> 00:00:49.549
You took a knee—explain to me how that season played out for you.

00:00:50.175 --> 00:00:51.426
- I could give you a story: 

00:00:51.426 --> 00:00:55.722
We are in a team meeting room, and...Coach Pagano 

00:00:55.722 --> 00:00:57.807
gets up and says, “Look, guys. 

00:00:57.807 --> 00:01:00.393
I know you guys all wanna do somethin’. 

00:01:00.393 --> 00:01:02.187
I don’t want you guys takin’ a knee.”

00:01:02.187 --> 00:01:04.272
Like, “What? Don’t take a knee?” 

00:01:04.272 --> 00:01:05.774
Like, “Whatchu mean, not take a knee?”

00:01:06.232 --> 00:01:07.275
He’s like, “Well, guys, look. 

00:01:07.275 --> 00:01:09.652
When we go out on the football field, it’s about football.”

00:01:09.652 --> 00:01:10.236
- Mmm.

00:01:10.236 --> 00:01:12.280
- I say, “So, but—” 

00:01:12.280 --> 00:01:14.616
And I turned around to some of the guys 

00:01:14.616 --> 00:01:16.993
and I, and I spoke to ‘em. I’m just like, “So, 

00:01:16.993 --> 00:01:20.663
when it’s about leukemia and your cancer, it’s cool. 

00:01:21.206 --> 00:01:25.335
But when it’s about police brutality and social injustice, 

00:01:26.336 --> 00:01:28.463
it’s not cool,” you know what I’m sayin’?

00:01:28.463 --> 00:01:30.507
And I told Chuck Pagano that. 

00:01:30.507 --> 00:01:31.966
You know, I’m just like, “Man, that’s, that’s—”

00:01:31.966 --> 00:01:33.676
I told him straight up, “That’s bullshit.” 

00:01:33.885 --> 00:01:36.888
You know, it’s, it’s, ”Oh, you know, football is bigger than, 

00:01:36.888 --> 00:01:38.056
bigger than what’s goin’ on the outside.”

00:01:38.056 --> 00:01:39.015
No, it ain’t. 

00:01:39.015 --> 00:01:40.141
How about respecting the guys 

00:01:40.141 --> 00:01:42.310
that’s gettin’ murdered and killed by police officers? 

00:01:42.310 --> 00:01:44.521
And not sayin’ that all police officers are bad. 

00:01:44.521 --> 00:01:47.398
But you get some, they get that—they get a lil’ power in their hand, 

00:01:47.398 --> 00:01:48.691
and they abuse the power.

00:01:48.691 --> 00:01:50.819
I have six sons. You know what I’m sayin’? 

00:01:50.819 --> 00:01:52.779
Like, what if my son was in the car? 

00:01:52.779 --> 00:01:55.073
Or what if my son was walkin’ around? 

00:01:55.073 --> 00:01:57.575
And he get, and he get shot? 

00:01:57.575 --> 00:01:58.827
Over nothin’?

00:01:58.827 --> 00:02:00.495
So, that was my logic. 

00:02:00.495 --> 00:02:01.913
That was my thinkin’ into it. 

00:02:01.913 --> 00:02:04.582
Not because, “Oh, you know, it’s, it’s the NFL.”

00:02:04.707 --> 00:02:06.417
- Take me through the day when you took a knee. 

00:02:06.417 --> 00:02:08.044
Who were you playing, what week was it?

00:02:08.044 --> 00:02:10.421
- Week 3, Week 4 is when I took a knee. 

00:02:10.421 --> 00:02:12.340
Cuz I actually wanted a little more detail.

00:02:12.340 --> 00:02:16.344
I wanted to ask my grandfather about it, who served in the Marines. 

00:02:16.344 --> 00:02:19.722
Uh, talked to some family members that actually was, you know, 

00:02:19.722 --> 00:02:22.433
that was part—that was in the Army, and do they feel—

00:02:22.433 --> 00:02:25.770
did they feel, like, in it, was there any disrespect, you know? 

00:02:25.770 --> 00:02:28.064
And the biggest thing that came out was like, “No. 

00:02:28.064 --> 00:02:31.192
We don’t agree with it, but our thing is, 

00:02:31.192 --> 00:02:33.027
that’s what we, that’s what we fought for.”

00:02:33.027 --> 00:02:33.653
- Yeah.

00:02:33.653 --> 00:02:34.028
- You know what I’m sayin’? 

00:02:34.028 --> 00:02:36.698
“We fought for you to, to serve that purpose, 

00:02:36.698 --> 00:02:39.993
to go out and protest and have that freedom of speech 

00:02:39.993 --> 00:02:41.119
and everything else.” 

00:02:41.119 --> 00:02:44.581
So Week 3, we playin’ the San Diego Chargers. 

00:02:44.581 --> 00:02:47.083
I can remember me right before the national anthem, 

00:02:47.083 --> 00:02:48.585
first time I took a knee. 

00:02:48.585 --> 00:02:52.714
And what’s funny is, two or three of the executive guys 

00:02:52.714 --> 00:02:55.049
were standing behind me, and they was like, 

00:02:55.049 --> 00:02:57.677
“Cro, get up!” I was like, “Man, fuck y’all! I’m not gettin’ up!”

00:02:57.677 --> 00:02:58.636
- Wow, they told you that?

00:02:58.636 --> 00:02:59.596
- Yeah, they said, “Get up.” 

00:02:59.596 --> 00:03:01.306
What they end up doin’ was, 

00:03:01.306 --> 00:03:03.933
one guy was standing here, one guy was standing here, 

00:03:03.933 --> 00:03:06.144
one guy was standing here, and another guy was standing here. 

00:03:06.144 --> 00:03:09.272
One person even had a towel to try to block it, 

00:03:09.272 --> 00:03:10.690
you know, for nobody wantin’ to take a picture, 

00:03:10.690 --> 00:03:12.233
but they already had took a picture.

00:03:12.483 --> 00:03:14.819
- And then, Week 4, we are in London. 

00:03:15.737 --> 00:03:17.322
So we’re playin’ in London.

00:03:17.322 --> 00:03:17.906
- Mhmm.

00:03:17.906 --> 00:03:20.366
- And they came up to me before the game and 

00:03:20.366 --> 00:03:22.202
was like, “Hey, Cro, please don’t take a knee.”

00:03:22.202 --> 00:03:24.412
It’s like, “Man, y’all better get out my face.” 

00:03:24.412 --> 00:03:26.080
You know, y’all not fittin’ to sit here and tell me 

00:03:26.080 --> 00:03:27.999
what I can and cannot do. 

00:03:27.999 --> 00:03:29.792
I got, actually got benched that game. 

00:03:29.792 --> 00:03:33.922
I got pulled out, halftime, and didn’t play the second half at all.

00:03:34.797 --> 00:03:35.506
- Why was that?

00:03:36.507 --> 00:03:37.717
- They say it was cuz of my play, 

00:03:37.717 --> 00:03:39.636
but I was like, “You gave up four, four—” 

00:03:39.636 --> 00:03:42.263
I said, “You give up four catches for 35 yards 

00:03:42.263 --> 00:03:43.932
and a one-yard touchdown off a turnover 

00:03:43.932 --> 00:03:45.350
that your quarterback threw?” 

00:03:46.017 --> 00:03:46.893
C’mon, man.

00:03:46.893 --> 00:03:48.519
Two days after I took a knee

00:03:48.519 --> 00:03:50.021
I get like three or four phone calls. 

00:03:50.021 --> 00:03:52.065
I’m like, “Hey, who the hell these people 

00:03:52.065 --> 00:03:52.982
that’s callin’ my phone?” 

00:03:52.982 --> 00:03:53.942
I don’t recognize the number, 

00:03:53.942 --> 00:03:54.943
so I ended up answering the phone. 

00:03:54.943 --> 00:03:55.944
It was like, “Hey, yo, you in the facility?” 

00:03:55.944 --> 00:03:57.737
I was like, “Yeah, why? What’s up?”

00:03:57.737 --> 00:03:59.739
“Oh, uh, Chuck Pagano wanna see you.” 

00:03:59.739 --> 00:04:01.115
I was like, “All right, cool.” 

00:04:01.115 --> 00:04:02.033
So they come to get me. 

00:04:02.033 --> 00:04:03.993
It was like, “Uh, you got your playbook?”

00:04:05.119 --> 00:04:06.204
You know, I looked up like, 

00:04:06.204 --> 00:04:07.455
“What?! Do I got my playbook?”

00:04:07.455 --> 00:04:08.331
- Wow.

00:04:08.331 --> 00:04:10.458
- “Yeah, I got my playbook. Why?” 

00:04:10.458 --> 00:04:12.085
Now it’s like, “All right, cool. Lemme go talk to Chuck.” 

00:04:13.211 --> 00:04:16.714
So we get  in there, and he goes into this whole spiel: 

00:04:16.714 --> 00:04:18.841
“Uh, you know—hey, you know, 

00:04:18.841 --> 00:04:21.302
we’re releasing you because our guys are gettin’ healthy.”

00:04:21.302 --> 00:04:23.930
I’m like, “Dude, ain’t nobody healthy in the back end at all.” 

00:04:23.930 --> 00:04:25.265
It’s like, “Man, you ain’t gotta lie to me. 

00:04:25.265 --> 00:04:27.267
Just tell me the truth.” Only thing—only reason 

00:04:27.267 --> 00:04:29.227
I wanted him to say really what he would’ve said, 

00:04:29.227 --> 00:04:30.853
but he wouldn’t say it. I was like, so, 

00:04:30.853 --> 00:04:33.273
I was like, “So, wow, I’m gettin’ released for takin’ a knee?”

00:04:33.273 --> 00:04:35.275
He’s like, “Nah, you know, it’s not that.”

00:04:35.275 --> 00:04:36.067
- Mmm.

00:04:36.067 --> 00:04:37.235
- “You know, you just—you know, 

00:04:37.235 --> 00:04:38.569
we just feel like we gettin’ healthy.”

00:04:38.569 --> 00:04:39.028
- Yeah.

00:04:39.028 --> 00:04:40.238
- I said, “Man, y’all ain’t finna sit here and 

00:04:40.238 --> 00:04:42.407
just pay me three million damn dollars to now 

00:04:42.407 --> 00:04:45.410
to release me and then talkin’ about y’all just gettin’ healthy.”

00:04:45.410 --> 00:04:47.245
I said, “That don’t even make sense, Chuck.” 

00:04:47.245 --> 00:04:48.705
I said, “But it’s cool.”

00:04:48.705 --> 00:04:49.664
[Laughing]

00:04:49.664 --> 00:04:51.916
I said, yo, I said, “You boutta get fired anyway.” 

00:04:53.543 --> 00:04:54.544
Straight like that.

00:04:54.544 --> 00:04:55.545
- How’d he respond to that?

00:04:56.296 --> 00:04:59.299
- He ain’t say nothin’. He ain’t say nothin’. 

00:04:59.299 --> 00:05:00.925
And guess what, guess what end up happenin’? 

00:05:00.925 --> 00:05:01.551
- What happened?

00:05:01.551 --> 00:05:02.260
- He got fired. 

00:05:03.219 --> 00:05:04.679
Him and the damn GM.

00:05:05.054 --> 00:05:06.431
- How you think your decision to take a knee 

00:05:06.431 --> 00:05:07.515
affected your career?

00:05:07.765 --> 00:05:09.350
- Oh, it affected it big-time. 

00:05:09.350 --> 00:05:10.935
It ain’t have nothin’ to do with my age, 

00:05:10.935 --> 00:05:13.688
it ain’t have nothin’ to do with my style of play: 

00:05:13.688 --> 00:05:15.189
It was because I took a knee. 

00:05:15.189 --> 00:05:17.984
October 2nd was my last game. 

00:05:17.984 --> 00:05:21.487
I got one workout that whole entire time. 

00:05:21.487 --> 00:05:23.448
And that was by the Saints in 2017.

00:05:24.324 --> 00:05:25.533
- Do you regret that decision at all?

00:05:25.533 --> 00:05:26.284
- Nope. 

00:05:26.284 --> 00:05:30.913
Don’t regret it at all. Nah, don’t—why, why should I? 

00:05:30.913 --> 00:05:32.373
Cuz at the end of the day, only thing we did 

00:05:32.373 --> 00:05:35.251
was give people a voice that didn’t have a voice. 

00:05:35.251 --> 00:05:39.505
And it brought more attention to what really was goin’ on, 

00:05:39.505 --> 00:05:41.049
and now everyone’s talkin’ about it. 

00:05:41.049 --> 00:05:43.843
But there’s still no solution because it’s still goin’ on. 

00:05:43.843 --> 00:05:47.180
What’s crazy about that is, we got death threats.

00:05:48.014 --> 00:05:50.183
Death threats really don't matter to me.

00:05:50.183 --> 00:05:50.600
[Laughing]

00:05:50.600 --> 00:05:52.852
It was, like, but—it's just, like, you know,

00:05:52.852 --> 00:05:55.688
you get guys that say they’re about somethin’ 

00:05:55.688 --> 00:05:57.482
and they wanna stand for somethin’. 

00:05:57.482 --> 00:05:58.816
But they won’t do nothin’. 

00:05:58.816 --> 00:06:00.902
The NFL is 75 percent black. 

00:06:00.902 --> 00:06:03.529
If all black players walked off the field one day, 

00:06:03.529 --> 00:06:04.489
what they gonna have? 

00:06:06.199 --> 00:06:07.075
You know what I’m sayin’? 

00:06:07.075 --> 00:06:10.119
How much money will they lose if you stand together?

00:06:13.122 --> 00:06:14.374
Thanks for kickin' it with us.

